      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T14:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like it could be solved in a better way. `all-framework-module-impl` is only used by a single module, which doesn\u0027t compile against the SDK, so there\u0027s no requirement that all-framework-module-impl needs to compile against the SDK.\n\nCan you create two libraries:\n\n1) updatable-framework-module-impl with static libs { updatable modules }\n2) all-framework-module-impl with static libs { updatable-framework-module-impl, non-updatable-framework-module1, non-updatable-framework-module2 }\n\n#1 should compile against module_current, #2 doesn\u0027t have to.\n\nThis way, no \"custom\" entry within the Android.bp is necessary.",
